Prompt Level: 7.0 Prompt: Your teacher has asked you to write a short text about the parts of an airplane. Explain what each of the different parts are for, including the fuselage, wings, tail and engines. Write 150-200 words. Response: Airplane parts:

- fuselage: is the body of the airplane, where the passengers are located. In addition,  it includes the cockpit, where the pilot and the first officer operate, the cargo hold, where all the luggage is wedged in and the landing gear;
- wings: are the surfaces that sustain the airplane during flight. On the back edges of the wings there are ailerons, which are fundamentals for increasing or decreasing the drag during take off and landing;
- tail: it is located ant the end of the fuselage and it holds a rudder uses to make the airplane turn left or right. It can also have small flaps useful for stabilize the airplane during the flight;
- engines: engines are usually placed on the wings and are use to generate the power needed by the airplane to move and flight. Most aircraft engines are either piston engines or gas turbines, although a few have been rocket powered and in recent years many small UAVs have used electric motors.

Prompt Level: 7.0 Prompt: Your boss has sent you an email, asking you to prepare a presentation about the company. Read the email and draft a speech. Include an introduction, a body (with signposting phrases, where possible), an anecdote and a call to action. Write 150–250 words. Response: As you know, I need your help preparing a short presentation about the company for recruits. Can you write up a short speech?  Try to make it engaging; i don't want just a boring list of facts. Some key points to include:
1. Frisko Shipping was founded in 2001 by Bill Frisko;
2.locations in 20 cities all over the world;
3.more than 5,000 employees;
4.our profit of 5 million dollars last year and 10 percent of the global market;
5.New employees are expected to be motivated and enthusiastic.
It might be useful to hold a quiz too see how much they already know about the company.
They might want to know something about me, so you can tell them about the time that the passing ship that saved my life inspired me to start my own shipping company. Hopefully they'll see that as evidence that they can find inspiration anywhere.

Prompt Level: 10.0 Prompt: Read the email from your manager. Then respond with an email that has several ideas to help her solve the budget problem. Type in the input box. Write between 80 and 100 words. Use your own words where possible. Response: Hi Carla, how are you ?

I have some ideas for cutting costs for the budget crisis, like:
- Negotiation with suppliers: Renegotiate contracts for better prices and deadlines;
- Purchase in larger volumes: Get discounts due to economies of scale;
- Process automation: Reduce manual tasks with management software and artificial intelligence;
- Just-in-time: Avoid excessive inventory and minimize waste;
- Digital marketing: Use organic strategies instead of excessively paid advertising.

I hope this ideas could help, 
Bye

Prompt Level: 7.0 Prompt: Listen again to the flight attendant. Type out the whole text of the recording. Compare your text with the model. Response: This is about a flight assistant, who is in charge of:
- Serve the passengers and ensure their safety;
- Help the passengers to find their seats and put their carry on baggage on the over head compartments;
- Make an inventory off all supplies: blankets, food and beverage;
