- Providing greater ROI; 
= Making company more efficient; 
- Cost of loss; 
- More savings; 
-Reducing manual checks and others aspects.

Prompt Level: 13.0 Prompt: You are writing to Harry, a new manager in your company. He wants advice on how to effectively motivate his team and what strategies to avoid. Use the language and strategies you have learned in this lesson. Type in the input box. Write 150-200 words. Response: Hi Harry,
How are you?
I will pinpoint here some of my ideas to motivate my team:
- The empolyees have to feel that they are part of something, it is very important to show them the purpose of their job;
- Don't be agressive in the goals setting, always incentivate and encourage your employees and let them surprise you with a higher performance;
- Be sincere during the performance assessement, valuing the achieviments and giving advices on the points that needs to be improved;
- Always reward the employees when an important goal is acheived or a project is delivered. It is a substancial motivation;
- do never, ever, be rude. If something frustrates you, take a moment to breath and think how to comunicate it to the employee;
- If the employee is not succed in something, let this person reflect on that, do not give an imediate feedback, the person can be reactive. Wait 1 or 2 days to talk about it and contribute with some ideas to solve the situation.

Good luck!!!!

Prompt Level: 7.0 Prompt: You have plans to meet again with the prospective car dealership owner later this week in hopes of closing the deal. To help prepare for the meeting, take notes as your boss describes the current state of the automotive industry. Pay particular attention to what she says about customer preferences, current industry trends, and your company's strategy. Response: Customer preferences - family prefer roomier vehicles and minivan; single men prefer sport-car and convertible;

Current industry trends - all these models have better fuel efficiency than in the past, HEVs are available and they are better that conventional vehicles in terms of oil consumption and exhausting;

Company's strategy - Joint international venture between all 11 Ford, GM and Chrysler, customer have the opportunity to go to the dealer shop to looking for a car which answer to its request.

Prompt Level: 13.0 Prompt: You are writing to Harry, a new manager in your company. He wants advice on how to effectively motivate his team and what strategies to avoid. Use the language and strategies you have learned in this lesson. Type in the input box. Write 150-200 words. Response: Hi Harry,
Hope you are doing well. We are really happy that you joined our management team. According to your question, I would be happy to share our advices how we are motivating our teams in our company.
Here is some tips and tricks what could be used:
*Create a clear  and possible to achieve goals and share your expectations on the deliveries;
*Provide regular feedback, which will help team members understand their strengths and areas for improvements;
*Empower your team, giving them autonomy to make decisions and take ownership of their work;
*Always celebrate successes, even small achievements! As this boosts morale and motivation;
*Communicate effectively and in understandable way
Also it is important to note what you should try to avoid:
*Micromanaging is not the best idea, as people don't like to be controlled in each step;
*Avoid difficult conversations
*Overpromise and underdeliver
Hope these tips help you navigate your new role as a manager and inspire your team to achieve great things! If you have any specific questions or need further advice, feel free to ask.

Best regards,
J.

